jobs.description:
Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.

Looking for a job with fixed hours and want to work with a big logistics company? Look no further and apply now! You'll be working in a large warehouse in Wijchen, part of an international logistics organisation. From four warehouses on the same site, large volumes of goods go out every day to customers across Europe and beyond. Your work keeps that moving. You operate the EPT and make sure pallets get to the right place. You do that independently and accurately. When things get busy somewhere, you pitch in on another task. Nothing complicated, just doing your job well.

 - Proven, recent hands-on experience operating an EPT;
 - Available in dayshift Monday to Friday, 40 hours per week;
 - You speak and understand Dutch or English.

The position
As an electrician, you will work in a team of over 40 technicians as part of Technical Services. You will independently carry out repairs, maintenance, commissioning and periodic safety inspections of electrical construction machinery and/or aerial work platforms so that they can be used optimally, efficiently and functionally.

Your tasks and responsibilities

  - Troubleshooting;

  - Analysing malfunctions;

  - Troubleshooting faults using electronic and hydraulic diagrams;

  - Performing maintenance checks;

  - Performing repairs;

  - Performing on-site inspections;

  - Keeping workplace/environment clean and tidy.

Our offer

  - Market-based salary and working conditions according to the Collective Labour Agreement for Metalworking;

  - We have a 40-hour working week and, according to the collective labour agreement, you can choose between the full commutation of ADV or 13 ADV days per year;

  - Discounts on products and services with the Employee Benefit Programme;

  - Free access to SnowWorld;

  - Holiday pay, training opportunities, bicycle plan, fitness plan, overtime compensation (free time or money), ...;

  - 26-leave days and the possibility to buy an additional 8 leave days;

  - Monthly Friday afternoon drinks in our in-house café;

  - The opportunity to attend various events for free;

  - Being part of our informal Collé family.

Your profile.

  - MBO working and thinking level, obtained through a technical education such as mechatronics or agricultural mechanisation;

  - Technical knowledge, experience and insight in the field of electro and hydraulics;

  - Problem-solving and analytical skills, service-oriented;

  - Sense of responsibility, flexible, independent and also a team player;

  - Sufficient command of the Dutch language. We also invite suitable candidates with a command of the English and/or German language who are willing to learn Dutch;

  - Living in the Sittard region.

Interested?
Don't wait any

In a modern 13,500 m² warehouse, millions of order lines are processed each year. As an Order Picker using an Order Pick Truck (OPT), you play a key role in ensuring customer orders are collected accurately and on time. If you enjoy working actively in a fast-paced logistics environment, this could be the right opportunity for you.
Acerca de la empresaThis international B2B specialist in mobility accessories is a leading player in the Benelux with strong international ambitions. From a highly automated distribution center, over two million order lines are processed annually. The warehouse features an advanced OSR shuttle system, modern internal transport equipment, and dedicated ADR compartments for hazardous goods storage. Efficiency, safety, and quality are central within the logistics team.
Sobre el trabajoAs an Order Picker, you work independently within the picking aisles using an Order Pick Truck (OPT). You collect orders according to the Warehouse Management System (WMS) and check items for correct quantities and quality. Once completed, you prepare orders for shipment to ensure customers receive their products on time.
 You are also responsible for replenishing pick locations using internal transport equipment and identifying stock discrepancies. Maintaining a clean and safe work environment is essential, and you report any unsafe situations when necessary. You may also assist with loading activities when required. This is a full-time role in a 2-shift system with the following times:
 6:00 - 15:00 & 15:00 - 0:00.
Requisitos - MBO-level working and thinking ability;
 - Experience with an OPT, EPT, or similar internal transport equipment is a plus;
 - Physically fit and comfortable with active work;
 - Good command of the English language;
 - Accuracy and attention to detail;
 - Ability to handle workload and work under pressure;
 - Able to work independently and as part of a team;
 - Strong focus on working safely.
 - EU nationality.

Qué ofrecemos -

Would you like to work as a warehouse employee in a friendly and supportive team? At our client's site in Heijen, you'll play a vital role in the logistic supply for fashion and high-tech. Your responsibilities will include collecting, scanning, and verifying orders.

Career Growth Opportunities

Do you have ambition, a desire to learn, and a vision for your future? Then this role is a great fit. We offer clear growth paths toward positions such as Line Lead, Assistant Supervisor, or Supervisor. There is also the opportunity to transition into a direct contract with Arvato.

Apply Now

Interested in joining the team? Click the apply button, and we’ll get in touch as soon as possible to explore the possibilities together!

Requirements:

- Experience with a hand scanner is a plus;

- Good command of English (speaking, reading, and writing);

- Able to provide a Certificate of Conduct (VOG);

- Experience in logistics is a plus but not a requirement;

- Own accommodation is required;

Fleet Planner
As a fleet planner at Van den Bosch Iberia in Barcelona (Spain), your responsibilities lie in the daily management of our drivers. You will be part of Team Trucking at our Barcelona office and with your fellow fleet planners and truck planners. Together with the other planners, you will be responsible for the operational coordination of international transports within Spain, Portugal and southern France.

We are Van den Bosch – The Supply Changer in Bulk. We believe bulk logistics can be approached smarter. Our mission is to create sustainable and tangible change in the sector through innovation, passion, expertise, and ambition.

As part of that mission, you will play a key role in making our smart bulk logistics a reality. You are responsible for your own group of drivers and trucks. You ensure that both productivity and quality of work are continuously improved. In close cooperation with the Truck Planners you translate the schedules to the drivers so that the trips are executed as efficiently as possible. You will also work with the customer service and master planning team to ensure a smooth operational flow. A proactive attitude and clear communication are therefore indispensable. You make our fleets run as efficiently as possible!

Knowledge of bulk transport is nice to have, but this is not a requirement. To get to know Van den Bosch and our industry, you will participate in the extensive induction programme at our headquarters in the Netherlands. After this is completed, you will join your colleagues to start working on your own. In this position, it is important that you are strong and can switch quickly to keep the operation running.

